<title>FRANCE: Scor climbs on 1996 profit jump.</title>
<headline>Scor climbs on 1996 profit jump.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French reinsurer Scor hit a record high in early trade before retracing slightly after reporting a 20 percent jump in 1996 profits and doubling its dividend.</p>
<p>At 1105 GMT, shares were up 2.61 percent at 243.0 francs after touching an all-time peak of 252.0 francs earlier.</p>
<p>Scor posted profits of 624 million francs, up from 522 million and doubled its net dividend to 10 francs.</p>
<p>Company chairman Jacques Blondeau said 1997 had started well. &quot;We don't see any particular reason why 1997 should be any different from 1996,&quot; Blondeau said, but declined to say whether 1997 profits would show the same percent rise as 1996.</p>
</text>
